# Skill: Add Feature

## When to use this skill

Use when adding a new domain entity (e.g. a new content type like "Inspections") or a complete new workflow spanning data model, API, and UI.

For adding a single API endpoint to an existing domain, use the `add-api-endpoint` skill instead.

---

## Step-by-step workflow

### Step 1 — Define shared types

File: `src/types/index.ts`

Add the new entity's public interface used by UI components. This is the client-facing shape.

```typescript
export interface Inspection {
  id: ID;
  listingId: ID;
  studentId: ID;
  scheduledAt: string;
  status: 'pending' | 'confirmed' | 'cancelled';
  createdAt: string;
}
```

Also add form types if needed:

```typescript
export interface InspectionForm {
  listingId: ID;
  scheduledAt: string;
}
```

### Step 2 — Create the Mongoose model

File: `src/lib/db/models/<ModelName>.ts`

Follow the model conventions exactly:

1. Define `as const` enum objects for status fields
2. Define the `IModelName` Document interface
3. Define the `IModelNameModel` static methods interface
4. Build the Mongoose schema with validation
5. Add compound indexes that match expected query patterns
6. Add the hot-reload guard on export
7. Export a type-safe model instance

```typescript
// Abbreviated example
import mongoose, { Schema, Document, Model } from 'mongoose';

export const InspectionStatus = {
  PENDING: 'pending',
  CONFIRMED: 'confirmed',
  CANCELLED: 'cancelled',
} as const;
export type InspectionStatusType = (typeof InspectionStatus)[keyof typeof InspectionStatus];

export interface IInspection extends Document {
  _id: mongoose.Types.ObjectId;
  listingId: mongoose.Types.ObjectId;
  studentId: mongoose.Types.ObjectId;
  scheduledAt: Date;
  status: InspectionStatusType;
  isDeleted: boolean;
  deletedAt?: Date;
  createdAt: Date;
  updatedAt: Date;
}

export interface IInspectionModel extends Model<IInspection> {
  findActiveById(id: string): Promise<IInspection | null>;
}

const InspectionSchema = new Schema<IInspection, IInspectionModel>(
  { /* fields */ },
  { timestamps: true, toJSON: { virtuals: true, transform: (_doc, ret) => { ret.id = ret._id?.toString(); delete ret._id; delete ret.__v; return ret; } } }
);

// Indexes
InspectionSchema.index({ studentId: 1, isDeleted: 1 });
InspectionSchema.index({ listingId: 1, isDeleted: 1 });

// Static methods
InspectionSchema.statics.findActiveById = function(id: string) {
  return this.findOne({ _id: id, isDeleted: false });
};

const Inspection: IInspectionModel =
  (mongoose.models.Inspection as IInspectionModel) ||
  mongoose.model<IInspection, IInspectionModel>('Inspection', InspectionSchema);

export default Inspection;
```

Export from `src/lib/db/models/index.ts`:

```typescript
export { default as Inspection } from './Inspection';
```

### Step 3 — Create server-side Zod validators

File: `src/lib/validators/inspections.server.ts`

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod';

export const createInspectionSchema = z.object({
  listingId: z.string().min(1),
  scheduledAt: z.string().datetime(),
});
export type CreateInspectionInput = z.infer<typeof createInspectionSchema>;
```

Create the client-side validator too:

File: `src/lib/validators/inspections.ts`

```typescript
import { z } from 'zod';

export const inspectionFormSchema = z.object({
  listingId: z.string().min(1, 'Listing is required'),
  scheduledAt: z.string().min(1, 'Date is required'),
});
export type InspectionFormValues = z.infer<typeof inspectionFormSchema>;
```

### Step 4 — Create the service

File: `src/lib/services/inspections.service.ts`

- All functions `async`, all start with `await connectDB()`
- Return typed plain interfaces, not Mongoose documents
- Throw `Error` with descriptive messages for known failures

### Step 5 — Create API route(s)

Follow the `add-api-endpoint` skill for each route. Summary:
- `src/app/api/inspections/route.ts` — GET (list), POST (create)
- `src/app/api/inspections/[id]/route.ts` — GET (single), PATCH, DELETE

### Step 6 — Add OpenAPI schemas

File: `src/lib/openapi/schemas/inspections.ts`

Add JSDoc comments or schema objects. Register in `src/lib/openapi/index.ts`.

### Step 7 — Add query keys

File: `src/lib/query/keys.ts`

```typescript
inspections: {
  all: ['inspections'] as const,
  list: (filters: Record<string, unknown>) => [...queryKeys.inspections.all, 'list', filters] as const,
  detail: (id: string) => [...queryKeys.inspections.all, 'detail', id] as const,
  mine: () => [...queryKeys.inspections.all, 'mine'] as const,
}
```

### Step 8 — Create TanStack Query hooks

File: `src/hooks/api/useInspections.ts`

Follow the pattern in `useListings.ts` and `usePayments.ts`. Export from `src/hooks/api/index.ts`.

### Step 9 — Build UI components

Determine placement per `nextjs-patterns.mdc`:
- Detail display component: `src/components/inspections/InspectionDetailClient.tsx`
- Form component: `src/components/inspections/InspectionForm.tsx`
- Shared status badge: reuse `src/components/shared/Badge.tsx`

### Step 10 — Create page(s)

Files: `src/app/inspections/page.tsx`, `src/app/inspections/[id]/page.tsx`, etc.

Add server-level metadata where appropriate. Keep page files thin — delegate client logic to `*Client.tsx` components.

---

## Checklist

- [ ] Types defined in `src/types/index.ts`
- [ ] Mongoose model created with hot-reload guard, indexes, and soft-delete fields
- [ ] Model exported from `src/lib/db/models/index.ts`
- [ ] Zod validators created (`.server.ts` and `.ts`)
- [ ] Service created (all functions return typed plain objects)
- [ ] API routes created (named exports, guards, safeParse, response helpers)
- [ ] OpenAPI schema added
- [ ] Query keys added to `src/lib/query/keys.ts`
- [ ] TanStack Query hooks created and exported from `index.ts`
- [ ] UI components created in feature-specific directory
- [ ] Pages created (thin, delegate to client components)
- [ ] `npm run typecheck` passes

